  "native_quirks": {
    "unicode_name_encoder":"Native C-Gate measures the UTF-8 byte length, then maps every signed negative Java byte to FF through its hex helper. Five U+00E9 characters therefore encode as ten FF bytes: 05C0008C0000FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF. The C-Gate command boundary preserves this behavior; the raw protocol codec does not corrupt inbound bytes.",
    "closed_network":"Native C-Gate returned 200 even when the network was closed and wrote no frame. cmqttd deliberately requires a positive correlated PCI confirmation and fails closed instead."
  },
  "acceptance_boundary":"A cmqttd 200 response establishes correlated PCI-confirmed broadcast delivery from the active PCI generation only. Media-device acceptance, durable player state, bridged routing, and MQTT Media Transport entities are not claimed."
